sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Op as Operator
    participant K as Kernel
    participant NS as Namespaces
    participant CG as cgroup v2
    participant P as Process
    Op->>K: start a container
    K->>NS: unshare PID, net, mount, UTS, IPC
    NS-->>P: its own view of processes, interfaces, and filesystem
    Note over NS,P: namespaces decide what it can see
    K->>CG: place the process in a cgroup, write cpu.max and memory.max
    Note over CG,P: cgroups decide how much it can use
    P->>K: run
    loop while running
        CG->>K: account CPU, memory, and IO against the group
        alt over the memory ceiling
            K->>P: OOM kill within the group
        else over the CPU quota
            CG->>P: throttle until the next period
        end
    end
